From 3894de92f865ed6c463cfed48b729322c764e650 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:50:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix client switcher: neutral icon, per-client colors,
 drag-to-reorder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Clients rail button now shows a fixed DiceBear identicon instead of
the active client's own initials — it represents the switcher category,
not any one client. That distinction moves to the "My workspace" quick-
link pill below it, which now renders the active client's initials
avatar and matches the same zoom-on-hover/active treatment as the other
rail items instead of being a static text-only pill.

Client initials avatars were all rendering the same color regardless of
name — DiceBear's `initials` style needs an explicit backgroundColor
palette to vary by seed, so added one and each client now hashes to a
distinct color.

Dropdown panel and rows get back a small amount of border radius
(rounded-xl/rounded-lg) instead of being fully squared off. Each row now
has a 6-dot grip handle and real drag-and-drop reordering via native
HTML5 DnD, persisted per-browser in localStorage (no DB migration, since
drizzle-kit can't run in this sandbox to safely regenerate snapshot
metadata).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
